            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A taxi company charges an initial fee of $4 and $1.86 per kilometre travelled. Write a linear equation to model the cost, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "C",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", of a trip of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " kilometres.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$C=1.86x+4$, where $x\\geq0$ and $C$ is in dollars.",
      "worked": "The initial fee is the fixed cost, and the distance charge is $1.86x$ dollars.\n$$C=1.86x+4,\\qquad x\\geq0.$$\nThis assumes the stated rate applies throughout the trip and there are no additional charges.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
